From 04f99a725bc63343683b54dea1aa8f698c4c3b13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron Bockelie <aaronsb@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-09-21T22:40:50Z
Subject: [PATCH] camera stage 2: Hi847 ultrawide streams, session after session (kernel r23)

hi847-of.patch converts the ACPI-only Hi847 driver to device tree on the
hi846 pattern: hynix,hi847 compatible, vddio/vdda/vddd regulators, reset
and shutdown GPIOs, runtime-PM power on/off around MCLK with the stock
sequence (rails, 5 ms, MCLK 19.2 MHz, 8 ms, reset, 11 ms), a binding.
The board DTS adds the shared I/O LDO (gpio117) and the ultrawide LDO
(gpio109, vin from the I/O LDO), the MCLK1 pin state, cci0, the sensor on
cci0_i2c0 at 0x21 with both link frequencies, and the csiphy2 endpoint.
CONFIG_VIDEO_HI847=m. The sensor probes as hi847 5-0021 and tools/camtest.sh
captures 3264x2448 RAW10 at 30 fps; tools/raw2png.py decodes it. First
frame in docs/media/camera-uw-first-frame.jpg.

Only the first session per boot worked. The camera GDSC that collapsed
after a session never powered up again (status stuck at 'off', GDSCR
0x68282800, CFG_GDSCR 0x010e0000). A runtime bisect of the VFE power cycle
isolated vfe_set_clock_rates(): camcc-sm8450 registers every RCG with
clk_rcg2_ops, so after a session ife_0_clk_src, csid_clk_src, cphy_rx and
camnoc_axi still select PLL0/PLL3 outputs that are powered down, and the
GDSC power-up waits on clocks that never toggle, the case described on
clk_rcg2_shared_init(). camcc-sm8450-shared-rcg.patch switches all 35 RCGs
to clk_rcg2_shared_ops as camcc-sm8550 and camcc-sm8650 do; the RCGs park
on XO when disabled. Verified on r23: five consecutive sessions on VFE0 and
VFE1 at 30 fps, RCG CFG 0 after each. camcc-sm8450-retain-ff.patch adds
RETAIN_FF_ENABLE to the nine camera GDSCs, matching stock qcom,retain-regs.

Also: device-facts/camss-gdsc-2026-09-21 (camcc register dumps in three
states, diff, helpers), docs/11-camera.md, README Cameras row and two
flashing gotchas (modules live in the rootfs; a camera register touched
without its clock hangs the SoC), ADR-001 set Accepted (first frame on a
V4L2 node, its graduation rule). Measurement record in issue #27.

Source: https://github.com/aaronsb/sm-x800-linux/commit/04f99a725bc63343683b54dea1aa8f698c4c3b13
Local integration: extract only camcc-sm8450-retain-ff.patch; kernel diff unchanged.

---
clk: qcom: camcc-sm8450: set RETAIN_FF_ENABLE on the camera GDSCs

On the Galaxy Tab S8+ the first camera stream through CAMSS works and
TITAN_TOP collapses cleanly afterwards. The second stream fails with
"titan_top_gdsc status stuck at 'off'": GDSCR reads 0x68282000 and
CFG_GDSCR 0x010e0000, the power-up state machine started and never
reached power-up-complete.

The stock SM8450 device tree marks every camcc GDSC qcom,retain-regs,
which the downstream gdsc driver turns into GDSC_RETAIN_FF_ENABLE, and
the SM8550 camcc sets RETAIN_FF_ENABLE on all of its GDSCs. The SM8450
camcc sets it on none. Add it to all nine, matching stock.

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sm8450.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sm8450.c
index 4025db23d..d7c99e4b5 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sm8450.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sm8450.c
@@ -2933,7 +2933,7 @@ static struct gdsc bps_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "bps_gdsc",
 	},
-	.flags = HW_CTRL | POLL_CFG_GDSCR,
+	.flags = HW_CTRL | POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 	.parent = &titan_top_gdsc.pd,
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 };
@@ -2943,7 +2943,7 @@ static struct gdsc ipe_0_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "ipe_0_gdsc",
 	},
-	.flags = HW_CTRL | POLL_CFG_GDSCR,
+	.flags = HW_CTRL | POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 	.parent = &titan_top_gdsc.pd,
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 };
@@ -2953,7 +2953,7 @@ static struct gdsc sbi_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "sbi_gdsc",
 	},
-	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR,
+	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 	.parent = &titan_top_gdsc.pd,
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 };
@@ -2963,7 +2963,7 @@ static struct gdsc ife_0_gdsc = {
